575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-65038/selection/ac708c1f023392216b913bf2d51250dcc6f1dcd19190ca052730a2ee78d1fc67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-65038" :question/id #uuid "39f6ec50-e251-5f95-8416-ba7803d7b734" :question/math-academy-id "q-65038" :question/problem "Given that $D={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=2{x}^{3}+4?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}={x}^{2},{f}_{1}=-x,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2{x}^{3}+4)-x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+4) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{x}^{2})-x\\cdot 6{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 12x-6{x}^{3} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-6{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-65038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-65038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection/3a1b4446f31dbd94c9abf3647ed249d2b3776662186f9676b7bb96cdf3609296" :answer/id #uuid "5952ce3f-6d68-52c0-a877-1ef0389e6aa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection/bd2afdc0108fa68b0150a94333e66a7ccb838698c026d45978df86d3c3300979" :answer/id #uuid "96eb6d9c-b93b-5ffa-967d-6ffbd57dcc88" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection/1760d142dcb60d6ac0a156ebc6f58f2c565dcb90cbe7426e6ee99f00b49fd211" :answer/id #uuid "37c29747-2693-5054-ad6f-903b71a2720b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection/0e9ad8896b7f5791967b8c2923c7b926b47613f8015540fc686f693cad5339b4" :answer/id #uuid "f1ff5fef-dfc8-5f90-9e68-709ffa999b26" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection/1c6961163813a6e3b69ac0678fca4dc3447354e3e0240bbb5bdb5209e1893021" :answer/id #uuid "16335570-faa1-54a2-a02e-1201972d95b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed2b92a-d1ce-591e-a158-29fb029bd684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79607/selection/bd2afdc0108fa68b0150a94333e66a7ccb838698c026d45978df86d3c3300979" :answer-field/choices ["q-79607/selection/3a1b4446f31dbd94c9abf3647ed249d2b3776662186f9676b7bb96cdf3609296" "q-79607/selection/bd2afdc0108fa68b0150a94333e66a7ccb838698c026d45978df86d3c3300979" "q-79607/selection/1760d142dcb60d6ac0a156ebc6f58f2c565dcb90cbe7426e6ee99f00b49fd211" "q-79607/selection/0e9ad8896b7f5791967b8c2923c7b926b47613f8015540fc686f693cad5339b4" "q-79607/selection/1c6961163813a6e3b69ac0678fca4dc3447354e3e0240bbb5bdb5209e1893021"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79607" :question/id #uuid "1f384bed-894a-5dfa-9b9b-225075b79f42" :question/math-academy-id "q-79607" :question/problem "Given that $D=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=-1,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =(x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =x\\cdot (\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79607/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79607"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection/767463b8da5adee5ff3ccb9bc585f0a0eb083222b033211b6d93ca9563781f78" :answer/id #uuid "079a0fa3-a3f9-5751-bf95-f203bc4fb9ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "df9836fc-fe46-585c-a283-fc026f7d1c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection/9ef9d46a07e1d19cf967f0438e3a9ff631061bade57b40ff441734ea88edc528" :answer/id #uuid "a7814b1a-7112-5068-b556-d7e043539b8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection/1c7af01e0b38707f5a31a3b343bdafd556e5a9628313b487eeab6d978c50ba82" :answer/id #uuid "11b39f5e-f9fc-57ae-8282-27d5ad3dc10d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection/9da8c704d366fc5594fe81462ae2060df61e7036a770dfd6f418f2351dff624b" :answer/id #uuid "4723a33d-f6b6-5474-b89f-b0460010e71c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e145c1b5-0cad-5893-9b05-732087ad8dec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337845/selection/9ef9d46a07e1d19cf967f0438e3a9ff631061bade57b40ff441734ea88edc528" :answer-field/choices ["q-337845/selection/767463b8da5adee5ff3ccb9bc585f0a0eb083222b033211b6d93ca9563781f78" "q-337845/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-337845/selection/9ef9d46a07e1d19cf967f0438e3a9ff631061bade57b40ff441734ea88edc528" "q-337845/selection/1c7af01e0b38707f5a31a3b343bdafd556e5a9628313b487eeab6d978c50ba82" "q-337845/selection/9da8c704d366fc5594fe81462ae2060df61e7036a770dfd6f418f2351dff624b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337845" :question/id #uuid "ae2d10ba-6bbb-5ff9-ab97-ca3ddf449ad8" :question/math-academy-id "q-337845" :question/problem "Given that $D=2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=2x,{f}_{1}=3,$ and ${f}_{0}=4.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =(2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+4)\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+3(-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3/2}})+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\frac{3}{4{x}^{5/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}-\\frac{3}{2{x}^{3/2}}+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337845/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ff7f935-dcec-5b4c-ba1d-e0b4c9e197a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337845"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection/6ccc736e299da4ed07051c560d3e41bb145b2a48e6c4c914f983f345c142b5f3" :answer/id #uuid "a5db4e0c-8ac3-50a9-b223-6c4bc4ae57fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection/bf9881885b91c7ff143aee921857bed0d0bb65bafd8dc0c1f84b64de304a4989" :answer/id #uuid "06c8ac3d-ef08-52cd-98a6-a7e8dd73c82c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection/7cb3433636a7f308c15043fb8463de9ed0d15aa7b08c2982b7831b33551e4713" :answer/id #uuid "e197b1f1-6a27-58bb-bf85-f351f1623bb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2-2{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection/c1045d95c17b470e2d8a4a119ea64b3e0e12d52a8e736b277bdfaf826ecaa045" :answer/id #uuid "af46432a-3c50-5a4b-8e49-8037b8d5b9e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection/fbbc03783d573a542bb9b40c4cf8b9eb803ff92d6fcc586f3f5d0d2a5144fc20" :answer/id #uuid "8883c823-ac06-5254-8dc2-fbabda31a87f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}(2+{x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a2a7949-f7a7-5b03-85b0-65d7cffb972b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-337846/selection/6ccc736e299da4ed07051c560d3e41bb145b2a48e6c4c914f983f345c142b5f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-337846/selection/6ccc736e299da4ed07051c560d3e41bb145b2a48e6c4c914f983f345c142b5f3" "q-337846/selection/bf9881885b91c7ff143aee921857bed0d0bb65bafd8dc0c1f84b64de304a4989" "q-337846/selection/7cb3433636a7f308c15043fb8463de9ed0d15aa7b08c2982b7831b33551e4713" "q-337846/selection/c1045d95c17b470e2d8a4a119ea64b3e0e12d52a8e736b277bdfaf826ecaa045" "q-337846/selection/fbbc03783d573a542bb9b40c4cf8b9eb803ff92d6fcc586f3f5d0d2a5144fc20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-337846" :question/id #uuid "42241a9b-a6a8-5c40-bd12-92c20975f581" :question/math-academy-id "q-337846" :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+3{y}^{2},$ then $D({x}^{2})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-2xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=3y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{2}) & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({x}^{2})-2x({x}^{2})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+3({x}^{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)-2x({x}^{2})\\cdot 2x+3{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\cdot 2-4{x}^{4}+3{x}^{4} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}-{x}^{4} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-337846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-337846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-338253"] :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=y,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(2-(x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-337559"] :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2},$ then $D({e}^{2x})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=y,{f}_{1}=-xy,$ and ${f}_{0}=2y.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={e}^{2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{2x}) & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{2x})-x({e}^{2x})\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{2x})+2({e}^{2x})^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{e}^{2x})-x{e}^{2x}\\cdot 2{e}^{2x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}\\cdot 4{e}^{2x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x}+2{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =6{e}^{4x}-2x{e}^{4x} \\\\  & =2{e}^{4x}(3-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-337986"] :question/problem "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y,$ then $D({x}^{3})=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=y,$ and ${f}_{0}=2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y={x}^{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({x}^{3}) & =x({x}^{3})\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({x}^{3})+{x}^{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{x}^{2})+{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}\\cdot 6+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{4}+3{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(3{x}^{2}+6x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection/fe7f81408c98eda70b1553a15db678b9be7ee35f561ca8c2d6032c97772f4bec" :answer/id #uuid "fe0584f1-0aae-50ac-b6e5-640ece58a243" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection/6e4b722b9f7cb46b99f35d8279b75b25427dc9135814c7266cbc7825e083f96f" :answer/id #uuid "fb8641b5-6ade-5521-b3db-ca0bab88c272" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection/ae43cdad09fe024043d50645f0aec78c102e04b268735cad53a97f4d3503cae9" :answer/id #uuid "a238c216-92e1-53f5-b4d6-87d88a93a1f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection/06431b8333736b05e65503e8c584b930defd8e117873c33a7bd301ce3b423655" :answer/id #uuid "5936ad5d-47c1-54c8-b496-760a09fa8130" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(6-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection/2ff69795ea0bc3390f15fb262011c126ec45e8bc669b70b2459e879e5e93c0d6" :answer/id #uuid "c93b093d-82c3-5b47-8a9a-c34b0321dc69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3+8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bde7448d-6255-54c0-936b-fe929ae4a8c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-338254/selection/ae43cdad09fe024043d50645f0aec78c102e04b268735cad53a97f4d3503cae9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338254/selection/fe7f81408c98eda70b1553a15db678b9be7ee35f561ca8c2d6032c97772f4bec" "q-338254/selection/6e4b722b9f7cb46b99f35d8279b75b25427dc9135814c7266cbc7825e083f96f" "q-338254/selection/ae43cdad09fe024043d50645f0aec78c102e04b268735cad53a97f4d3503cae9" "q-338254/selection/06431b8333736b05e65503e8c584b930defd8e117873c33a7bd301ce3b423655" "q-338254/selection/2ff69795ea0bc3390f15fb262011c126ec45e8bc669b70b2459e879e5e93c0d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338254" :question/id #uuid "b9314e42-73f2-5134-b5e1-c3785c0ac3fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-338254" :question/problem "If $D(y)=xy\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+3y,$ then $D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)=$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338254/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7066d712-f0a3-554f-9d10-3d6fe4b95a18"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6570"] :question/problem "Given that $D=\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}}+3 \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x}+5,$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=e^{- x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a second-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = a_{2}\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + a_{1}\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + a_0y\n$$\n\nwith constant coefficients  $a_2 = 1, a_1 = 3,$ and $a_0 = 5.$ \n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}+5){e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}({e}^{-x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{-x})+3\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+5{e}^{-x} \\\\  & =3{e}^{-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6571"] :question/problem "Given that $D=x^2\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}}{\\textrm d x^{3}}-5x \\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}}{\\textrm d x^{2}} +9\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm d x},$ what is $D(y)$ for $y=\\ln{x}?$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} + f_{2}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x)y.\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = x^2, f_2 = -5x, f_1 = 9,$ and $f_0 = 0.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(y) & =D(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x})\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)-5x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+9\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(\\frac{1}{x})-5x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})+9\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})-5x(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{5}{x}+\\frac{9}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-21785"] :question/problem "If $D(y)=y\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} - \\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x} + y^3,$ then calculate $D(e^{3x}).$" :question/worked-solution "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y) = f_{3}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{3}y}{\\textrm d x^{3}} +  f_{2}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm d^{2}y}{\\textrm d x^{2}} + f_{1}(x,y)\\dfrac{\\textrm dy}{\\textrm d x} + f_0(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith $f_3 = y,  f_2 = 0,  f_1 = -1,$ and $f_0 = y^2.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y = e^{3x}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D({e}^{x}) & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}({e}^{3x})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{3x})+{({e}^{3x})}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(3{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{e}^{3x})-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & =27{e}^{6x}-3\\cdot {e}^{3x}+{e}^{9x} \\\\  & ={e}^{3x}({e}^{6x}+27{e}^{3x}-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
